1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,138
Every package on the exam machine comes from a repository.

2
00:00:04,158 --> 00:00:07,313
If the system cannot reach one, nothing installs.

3
00:00:07,783 --> 00:00:11,795
In this video: configure access to RPM repositories.

4
00:00:16,315 --> 00:00:18,898
Here's the task, the way an exam would state it.

5
00:00:19,368 --> 00:00:22,377
Configure access to RPM repositories.

6
00:00:22,847 --> 00:00:27,311
We'll see where repositories are defined, build a small one of our own, add it,

7
00:00:27,331 --> 00:00:29,184
check it, and turn it off and on.

8
00:00:36,704 --> 00:00:37,895
First, the idea.

9
00:00:37,915 --> 00:00:43,120
A repository is a folder or web address that holds RPM package files,

10
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:47,436
plus a catalog called repodata that lists what is inside.

11
00:00:49,906 --> 00:00:54,944
A small text file ending in dot repo, in /etc/yum.repos.d,

12
00:00:54,964 --> 00:01:01,833
tells dnf where that address is. dnf reads the catalog and offers the packages.

13
00:01:07,353 --> 00:01:14,153
Repository definitions live in /etc/yum.repos.d. ls lists the files there.

14
00:01:14,173 --> 00:01:16,549
Each one ends in dot repo.

15
00:01:22,069 --> 00:01:25,230
head -n 12 shows the top of rocky.repo.

16
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:30,369
A name in square brackets starts each repository. Here, baseos.

17
00:01:36,889 --> 00:01:40,946
dnf repolist shows the repositories that are turned on:

18
00:01:40,966 --> 00:01:47,024
appstream, baseos, and extras. The id on the left is the name you use in commands.

19
00:01:53,544 --> 00:01:56,991
Add --all, and the disabled repositories show too.

20
00:01:57,011 --> 00:02:00,457
The list is long, so only the start is shown here.

21
00:02:07,977 --> 00:02:12,839
Now we build our own. A tool called createrepo_c writes the catalog.

22
00:02:12,859 --> 00:02:18,368
It isn't installed, so dnf install adds it. The download output is shortened.

23
00:02:26,888 --> 00:02:29,861
mkdir makes a folder called localrepo.

24
00:02:29,881 --> 00:02:34,272
dnf download saves a package file without installing it,

25
00:02:34,292 --> 00:02:38,132
and --destdir picks the folder. We download tree.

26
00:02:45,652 --> 00:02:50,371
createrepo_c on the folder builds the repodata catalog inside it.

27
00:02:50,391 --> 00:02:54,016
ls shows the package file and the repodata folder.

28
00:03:00,536 --> 00:03:06,444
dnf config-manager --add-repo writes the dot repo file for us.

29
00:03:06,464 --> 00:03:11,990
The address starts with file://, a folder on this machine.

30
00:03:12,010 --> 00:03:16,580
Web repositories use http or https the same way.

31
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:25,385
A new file appears. cat shows it:

32
00:03:25,405 --> 00:03:29,715
the id in brackets, a name, the baseurl, and enabled equals 1.

33
00:03:30,185 --> 00:03:33,557
And dnf repolist now lists four repositories.

34
00:03:41,077 --> 00:03:43,468
dnf repoinfo shows the details:

35
00:03:43,488 --> 00:03:48,524
enabled, one package, the base URL, and the file that defines it.

36
00:03:58,044 --> 00:04:04,445
--repo limits dnf to one repository. list available shows its packages: tree.

37
00:04:10,965 --> 00:04:17,112
To turn a repository off without deleting it, use --set-disabled with its id.

38
00:04:17,132 --> 00:04:21,036
It leaves the list. --set-enabled brings it back.

39
00:04:29,556 --> 00:04:35,417
Packages are normally checked against a signing key. The setting is gpgcheck.

40
00:04:35,437 --> 00:04:38,243
Our local repository has no key file,

41
00:04:38,263 --> 00:04:43,360
so --save and --setopt turn the check off for this repository only.

42
00:04:43,830 --> 00:04:47,282
cat now shows gpgcheck=0 added to the file.

43
00:04:47,302 --> 00:04:51,319
Never do this for a repository you do not control.

44
00:04:58,839 --> 00:05:02,275
Our five steps: task, demo, check, reboot, and your turn.

45
00:05:03,795 --> 00:05:07,297
The repository file is on disk, so it survives a reboot.

46
00:05:07,317 --> 00:05:09,876
We restart the lab, and it comes back up.

47
00:05:13,346 --> 00:05:17,785
After a fresh boot, dnf repolist still lists our repository.

48
00:05:25,305 --> 00:05:28,030
Your turn. Create a folder lab12repo.

49
00:05:28,050 --> 00:05:33,741
Download the package zip into it, build a repository there with createrepo_c,

50
00:05:33,761 --> 00:05:38,192
and add it with dnf config-manager. Make sure it is enabled.

51
00:05:40,662 --> 00:05:43,479
Run the checker, and try before you open the solution.

52
00:05:48,999 --> 00:05:52,883
Next up: Install and remove RPM software packages.

53
00:05:53,353 --> 00:05:56,256
Subscribe to follow the series, and let's keep going.
